WEBVTT

00:00:00.388 --> 00:00:06.560
Welcome to Branch Assist, a generative AI procedure assistant built for the supplied eleven-document branch operations exercise.

00:00:06.687 --> 00:00:12.145
This recorded walkthrough covers the complete employee workflow, the engineering behind it, and the evidence used to evaluate it.

00:00:12.272 --> 00:00:18.204
You will see genuine application interactions, exact source passages, follow-up questions, and cases where an answer needs review.

00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:19.489
Narration is synthetic.

00:00:19.616 --> 00:00:24.841
This is an interview prototype over the supplied Cayman Bank snapshot, with a Wells Fargo inspired presentation.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:28.057
It provides decision support and does not execute banking transactions.

00:00:29.054 --> 00:00:32.476
The workspace opens with guided scenarios and a place to ask your own question.

00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:36.066
The sidebar has three views: Workspace, Procedure library, and Evaluation.

00:00:36.193 --> 00:00:38.225
Search scope defaults to all eleven procedures.

00:00:38.352 --> 00:00:40.209
That supports exploration across topics.

00:00:40.336 --> 00:00:43.299
A narrower scope deliberately restricts retrieval to one procedure.

00:00:43.426 --> 00:00:49.035
All runtime retrieval and language-model inference happen on this computer; an external inference API is not required.

00:00:50.021 --> 00:00:51.420
The architecture has two paths.

00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:58.192
Offline preparation parses the eleven original HTML files, builds traceable passages, and creates lexical and semantic indexes.

00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:04.133
At runtime, a single orchestrator resolves the question, verifies the snapshot, retrieves and reranks passages, and gives bounded

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.748
evidence to the local generator.

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:09.032
Output checks determine whether to release, correct, or withhold the draft.

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:14.685
Retrieval augmented generation was chosen because procedural knowledge needs inspectable sources and explicit updates.

00:01:15.688 --> 00:01:20.814
The inputs contain narrative instructions and one hundred thirty-nine HTML tables, including nested tables.

00:01:20.941 --> 00:01:25.090
Structural parsing preserves headings, column labels, row conditions, and source locations.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.306
Table continuations repeat their conditions.

00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:32.221
Each passage carries its procedure, section, publication text, original file hash, and passage identity.

00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:35.213
Nearby qualifications can be included during evidence assembly.

00:01:35.339 --> 00:01:37.107
Linked external procedures are not fetched.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:41.406
This reduces lost context, but it does not guarantee that every relevant exception is retrieved.

00:01:42.388 --> 00:01:44.830
Hybrid retrieval combines two complementary signals.

00:01:44.957 --> 00:01:49.168
BM twenty-five matches exact terms, procedure identifiers, and specialized wording.

00:01:49.295 --> 00:01:51.790
MiniLM embeddings retrieve semantic paraphrases.

00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:56.886
Reciprocal rank fusion combines their rankings, and a cross encoder reranks the candidates jointly with the question.

00:01:57.013 --> 00:02:01.355
The generator usually receives up to three nonduplicate passages within a bounded evidence budget.

00:02:01.482 --> 00:02:04.219
Exact local vector search is sufficient for this small collection.

00:02:05.221 --> 00:02:09.333
We begin with a concrete question: what is the overnight storage limit for a coin-counting machine?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:15.323
The application resolves the topic, checks the source snapshot, retrieves evidence, and runs the local Qwen three, four billion

00:02:15.323 --> 00:02:15.940
parameter model.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:19.495
The answer shown is five thousand two hundred fifty dollars, with a source citation.

00:02:19.622 --> 00:02:21.128
That matches the supplied procedure.

00:02:21.255 --> 00:02:23.532
Generation is real, rather than a canned response.

00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:28.133
This recording shortens some pauses; the answer's measured runtime remains visible in the application.

00:02:29.121 --> 00:02:32.797
Clicking the citation selects that exact answer's source passage in the Evidence desk.

00:02:32.924 --> 00:02:38.021
The procedure is P R sixty-three, and the supplied text states the maximum overnight amount for a single machine.

00:02:38.148 --> 00:02:42.659
Citation labels belong to a particular answer; selecting an older answer selects its own record.

00:02:42.786 --> 00:02:44.711
A citation makes the answer inspectable.

00:02:44.838 --> 00:02:47.989
The reviewer still needs to check whether the quoted rule applies to the situation.

00:02:48.988 --> 00:02:55.190
Source provenance exposes the title, section anchor, passage identity, original filename, and SHA two-fifty-six fingerprint.

00:02:55.317 --> 00:02:58.655
The source-match badge checks the selected file against the supplied snapshot.

00:02:58.782 --> 00:03:02.128
Supported requests also recheck source files and cached-index fingerprints.

00:03:02.255 --> 00:03:06.622
A changed snapshot requires a rebuild rather than silently mixing old passages with new files.

00:03:06.749 --> 00:03:12.542
A publication date or matching hash identifies the snapshot; it does not certify that the document is currently authoritative

00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:12.846
policy.

00:03:13.854 --> 00:03:19.048
The optional Retrieval signals panel exposes lexical, semantic, and reranking scores for the selected passage.

00:03:19.175 --> 00:03:22.573
These are matching signals, not calibrated confidence that the answer is correct.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.669
An adjacent qualification inherits its originating hit's scores.

00:03:25.796 --> 00:03:31.232
The interface keeps these technical details available for inspection without turning them into an unsupported certainty percentage.

00:03:32.221 --> 00:03:35.303
The original procedure can be downloaded directly from the Evidence desk.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:39.686
That lets a reviewer inspect the complete source, including context outside the retrieved passage.

00:03:39.813 --> 00:03:45.730
This is especially useful when a short answer depends on several eligibility conditions or when a linked reference is outside the

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.293
supplied collection.

00:03:47.288 --> 00:03:50.122
The Checks view separates the release decision into concrete screens.

00:03:50.249 --> 00:03:55.737
Citation labels must exist, factual statements need attribution, and numbers must occur in their own cited passages.

00:03:55.864 --> 00:03:58.593
Recognized strict and inclusive thresholds are compared as well.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.178
Each screened statement has a source association and a supporting evidence window.

00:04:02.305 --> 00:04:06.606
Direct wording can use a verbatim match; paraphrases use a natural language inference classifier.

00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:09.108
These checks can miss errors or reject valid answers.

00:04:09.235 --> 00:04:13.745
Checks passed means the implemented screens passed, not that correctness has been independently established.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:20.447
Activity records the actions that actually ran: understand the request, verify the snapshot, retrieve, assemble evidence, draft,

00:04:20.447 --> 00:04:22.122
check, and choose the response.

00:04:22.249 --> 00:04:24.774
The stages carry measured durations and observed counts.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.322
If a correction happens, it appears as an additional action.

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:32.290
This is the agentic part of the experience: a bounded, observable workflow with a clear release decision.

00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:36.823
It is an execution record and deterministic decision summary, not the model's private chain of thought.

00:04:37.821 --> 00:04:43.659
The technical record exposes the trace identity, model, pipeline version, question resolution, generation attempts, and token

00:04:43.659 --> 00:04:44.023
counts.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.312
Download evidence record saves the selected response with its sources, checks, and activity.

00:04:48.439 --> 00:04:51.093
This provides a reproducible review artifact for the prototype.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:57.112
It is an opt-in download, rather than a production audit service with access control, redaction, retention, and centrally managed

00:04:57.112 --> 00:04:57.422
records.

00:04:58.421 --> 00:05:01.369
Now we ask: and is monthly testing done in single or dual control?

00:05:01.496 --> 00:05:05.924
The assistant identifies the related procedure but retrieves evidence for the newly requested task.

00:05:06.051 --> 00:05:07.338
It answers single control.

00:05:07.465 --> 00:05:13.577
Prior user questions help resolve conversational context; prior generated claims are not reused as authoritative evidence.

00:05:13.704 --> 00:05:17.870
Short histories and ambiguous pronouns remain a limitation of the deterministic resolver.

00:05:18.888 --> 00:05:21.578
The follow-up citation opens the monthly-testing passage.

00:05:21.705 --> 00:05:27.254
In the supplied procedure, monthly testing is single control, while weekly balancing and random monthly cash counts are dual

00:05:27.254 --> 00:05:27.546
control.

00:05:27.673 --> 00:05:29.590
The correct control level depends on the task.

00:05:29.717 --> 00:05:35.204
Inspecting this passage shows why keeping the same document scope is useful, but simply copying the earlier overnight-limit evidence

00:05:35.204 --> 00:05:36.648
would not answer the follow-up.

00:05:37.654 --> 00:05:39.723
Next we ask about savings bond redemption fees.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:45.706
With all procedures in scope, naming the new topic changes the retrieval target from coin machines to P R nineteen forty-nine.

00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:48.976
The supplied savings-bond procedure prohibits charging a redemption fee.

00:05:49.103 --> 00:05:51.124
Its citation belongs to this new response.

00:05:51.251 --> 00:05:55.138
Old passages are not silently carried into the Evidence desk as support for a new question.

00:05:56.154 --> 00:05:58.809
The Procedure library makes the supplied collection discoverable.

00:05:58.935 --> 00:06:01.191
Searching notary and pressing Enter filters the cards.

00:06:01.318 --> 00:06:06.159
A card shows the procedure identifier, title, publication information, section count, and passage count.

00:06:06.286 --> 00:06:09.218
The original document and source fingerprint are available here as well.

00:06:09.345 --> 00:06:12.540
Use in workspace selects that procedure as the actual retrieval scope.

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:15.743
It does not grant document entitlements or establish policy authority.

00:06:16.754 --> 00:06:20.146
With the notary procedure selected, we deliberately ask a coin-machine question.

00:06:20.272 --> 00:06:23.926
The application asks for a scope change instead of answering from a conflicting document.

00:06:24.053 --> 00:06:27.451
The Evidence desk does not display the old source as if it supports this request.

00:06:27.578 --> 00:06:29.804
Changing scope clears contextual topic history.

00:06:29.931 --> 00:06:35.156
New investigation clears the conversation and feedback, but retains the selected scope, so the scope selector should be checked

00:06:35.156 --> 00:06:36.532
before starting a different topic.

00:06:37.554 --> 00:06:42.652
We start a new investigation within notary services and ask whether a notary can notarize an emailed document.

00:06:42.779 --> 00:06:48.244
The supplied P R one thousand procedure prohibits notarizing documents sent by email, fax, mail, or text.

00:06:48.371 --> 00:06:53.985
The point of this example is conditional reasoning: a plausible explanation must not create permission that the source does not

00:06:53.985 --> 00:06:54.266
give.

00:06:55.254 --> 00:06:58.224
The follow-up asks what changes if the requester is physically present.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:07:03.359
According to the supplied procedure, physical presence does not remove the prohibition on documents sent electronically.

00:07:03.485 --> 00:07:06.494
The assistant must retain the original emailed-document situation.

00:07:06.621 --> 00:07:08.575
Review the response status as well as its source.

00:07:08.702 --> 00:07:14.655
If a draft is withheld, the original passage is still the reference; a source-only response should never be presented as a

00:07:14.655 --> 00:07:15.506
successful generated answer.

00:07:16.521 --> 00:07:21.504
Returning to all procedures, we ask for the savings bond redemption limit for an account open less than twelve months.

00:07:21.631 --> 00:07:27.315
The supplied procedure describes a daily aggregate redemption-value limit of one thousand dollars, with an eligibility exception.

00:07:27.442 --> 00:07:31.057
A useful answer needs the applicable condition, the amount, and the time basis.

00:07:31.184 --> 00:07:35.777
The evidence should also be reviewed for presence and account-eligibility requirements in the complete procedure.

00:07:36.754 --> 00:07:39.415
We then ask about eligibility for The Private Bank Experience.

00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:43.578
Here, the generated draft was withheld after one correction still failed the support checks.

00:07:43.705 --> 00:07:48.637
The displayed original passage contains the exception to the account-age-related limit for eligible customers.

00:07:48.763 --> 00:07:51.560
This does not imply exemption from every redemption requirement.

00:07:51.687 --> 00:07:53.965
This is a real source-review outcome in the recording.

00:07:54.092 --> 00:07:58.633
The evidence remains useful, while the withheld response is not counted as a successful generated answer.

00:07:59.621 --> 00:08:02.538
This is a recorded regression example, not another live interaction.

00:08:02.665 --> 00:08:06.168
The business-trust question produced a first draft saying two million dollars or less.

00:08:06.295 --> 00:08:10.844
The cited source required less than two million, so the comparator check rejected the inclusive boundary.

00:08:10.971 --> 00:08:13.602
Deterministic feedback requested exact threshold wording.

00:08:13.729 --> 00:08:17.931
One correction, using the same evidence, produced the strict less-than criterion and passed the checks.

00:08:18.058 --> 00:08:19.894
There is a maximum of two generation attempts.

00:08:20.021 --> 00:08:23.938
Further failure withholds the draft; the system does not keep searching for a convenient answer.

00:08:24.954 --> 00:08:30.052
Another recorded case asked about a noncustomer in Arizona requesting notarization of a non-bank document.

00:08:30.179 --> 00:08:33.276
Both drafts failed the support screen, and the response became source-only.

00:08:33.403 --> 00:08:39.866
The retrieved procedure contains an Arizona exception, so this is also a useful example of unnecessary withholding: the support

00:08:39.866 --> 00:08:41.907
classifier can reject plausible source-supported wording.

00:08:42.034 --> 00:08:45.199
The interface labels the withheld draft and preserves the source passages.

00:08:45.326 --> 00:08:51.080
Safety screening must be evaluated together with answer coverage and employee review effort, rather than describing every refusal as

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:51.685
a success.

00:08:52.688 --> 00:08:55.851
Back in the application, feedback is recorded against the selected response.

00:08:55.978 --> 00:08:59.391
Helpful or Needs review is session feedback, not automatic model retraining.

00:08:59.518 --> 00:09:05.372
Export investigation downloads the conversation, response records, sources, checks, activity, scope, and feedback as a structured

00:09:05.372 --> 00:09:05.738
file.

00:09:05.865 --> 00:09:08.309
The browser session should not be treated as permanent storage.

00:09:08.436 --> 00:09:13.156
Export before resetting, and handle any downloaded investigation according to the intended review process.

00:09:14.154 --> 00:09:17.936
After New investigation, the question, can they do that, has no usable situation.

00:09:18.062 --> 00:09:21.152
The application requests more context and shows no supporting passage.

00:09:21.279 --> 00:09:23.354
Earlier sources are not borrowed to fill the gap.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:27.142
A second independent browser session also starts without the first session's conversation.

00:09:27.269 --> 00:09:33.448
Session isolation is implemented, while enterprise authentication and durable conversation management remain outside this prototype.

00:09:34.454 --> 00:09:37.087
Asking about tomorrow's weather demonstrates the knowledge boundary.

00:09:37.214 --> 00:09:42.093
These operational procedures do not provide that information, so the application reports insufficient evidence.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:47.242
An unsupported outcome can also occur on a valid procedural question if retrieval or generation fails.

00:09:47.369 --> 00:09:52.557
It should therefore be reviewed as an observed outcome, not assumed to prove that the requested rule is absent from the

00:09:52.557 --> 00:09:53.052
original documents.

00:09:54.054 --> 00:09:58.474
An explicit question about an unavailable procedure is handled without inventing its requirements.

00:09:58.601 --> 00:10:00.708
Only the eleven supplied documents are evidence.

00:10:00.835 --> 00:10:06.275
External links are not silently followed, and the language model's general training knowledge is not an approved substitute for a

00:10:06.275 --> 00:10:06.819
missing procedure.

00:10:07.821 --> 00:10:12.121
A direct instruction to ignore previous instructions and reveal the system prompt is rejected.

00:10:12.247 --> 00:10:14.459
This demonstrates a narrow pattern-based input guard.

00:10:14.586 --> 00:10:20.601
It does not establish comprehensive protection against prompt injection, source poisoning, privacy failures, or unauthorized access.

00:10:20.728 --> 00:10:23.923
The demo uses hypothetical scenarios without customer identifiers.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:29.824
A production system would require document entitlements, stronger threat testing, approved data handling, and operational controls.

00:10:30.821 --> 00:10:33.430
The application is also checked at a narrow mobile viewport.

00:10:33.557 --> 00:10:38.000
The welcome screen remains usable without horizontal overflow, and the prototype label stays visible.

00:10:38.127 --> 00:10:40.885
This is an actual browser screenshot from a separate, empty session.

00:10:41.012 --> 00:10:46.162
On narrower layouts, the evidence area follows the conversation rather than competing for a desktop-sized side panel.

00:10:47.154 --> 00:10:50.763
Evaluation shows recorded results from the completed version two regression run.

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:55.875
Labelled evidence appeared in the top five for all thirty ordinary questions with hybrid retrieval and reranking.

00:10:56.002 --> 00:11:00.497
The generated-answer fact-group proxy passed twenty-three of thirty, or seventy-six point seven percent.

00:11:00.624 --> 00:11:04.203
Six of thirty-five evaluated generated calls became source-only outcomes.

00:11:04.329 --> 00:11:06.503
These figures describe different stages of the system.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:11.975
Finding the right passage does not guarantee that the generator preserves every condition or produces a complete answer.

00:11:12.988 --> 00:11:16.311
The labels were AI-authored and source-checked, not independently adjudicated.

00:11:16.438 --> 00:11:21.008
Keyword matching can miss a valid paraphrase or pass an incorrect answer containing expected terms.

00:11:21.135 --> 00:11:25.382
Two of four original final-turn follow-up checks passed; ambiguous questions remain a weakness.

00:11:25.509 --> 00:11:31.305
Median generated-call latency was thirteen point eight seconds, with a ninety-fifth percentile of twenty-three point nine, excluding

00:11:31.305 --> 00:11:32.328
cold model load.

00:11:32.455 --> 00:11:35.417
Nine corrections were attempted and two revised answers were released.

00:11:35.544 --> 00:11:41.228
Thirty-seven automated tests and browser checks verify mechanics and integration, not independent substantive accuracy.

00:11:42.221 --> 00:11:45.025
The next validation needs independent operational reviewers.

00:11:45.152 --> 00:11:48.558
Accuracy asks whether the guidance and conditions are correct for the situation.

00:11:48.685 --> 00:11:50.844
Relevance asks whether it answers the actual task.

00:11:50.971 --> 00:11:53.942
Completeness asks whether material conditions and exceptions are present.

00:11:54.068 --> 00:11:57.428
Conciseness asks whether the answer is useful without unnecessary detail.

00:11:57.555 --> 00:12:02.217
Two reviewers should score unseen scenarios and adjudicate disagreements, with critical errors tracked separately.

00:12:02.344 --> 00:12:08.873
Compare employee task completion and time to correct guidance against existing search, while measuring both unsupported answers and

00:12:08.873 --> 00:12:09.599
unnecessary refusals.

00:12:10.588 --> 00:12:15.806
The Evaluation view provides downloads for the evaluation report, detailed solution overview, and presentation.

00:12:15.932 --> 00:12:19.691
The submission archive contains presentation materials without implementation source.

00:12:19.817 --> 00:12:23.539
This video also shows the application and explanatory graphics without source code.

00:12:23.666 --> 00:12:29.832
Generative AI assisted requirements analysis, implementation, tests, regression-case drafting, and presentation preparation.

00:12:29.958 --> 00:12:32.363
Runtime answer generation is a separate model use.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:38.582
Source checks, automated tests, browser assertions, and recorded evaluation document validation; independent operational review

00:12:38.582 --> 00:12:39.452
remains pending.

00:12:40.454 --> 00:12:44.304
Before a real pilot, procedure owners need authoritative versions and supersession rules.

00:12:44.431 --> 00:12:47.949
Independent reviewers need to establish quality and risk-based release criteria.

00:12:48.076 --> 00:12:54.002
Engineering needs identity, document entitlements before retrieval, redacted audit records, concurrency controls, monitoring, and

00:12:54.002 --> 00:12:54.426
rollback.

00:12:54.553 --> 00:12:59.372
Stronger approved models should be compared on the same unseen scenario set, including cost and latency.

00:12:59.499 --> 00:13:02.619
The next decision is a scoped validation effort with operational owners.

00:13:02.746 --> 00:13:07.655
The current evidence does not justify unsupervised branch deployment or a claim of measured productivity savings.

00:13:08.654 --> 00:13:14.773
The complete workflow is now visible: ask a specific question, inspect the cited passage, review the checks and actual activity,

00:13:14.773 --> 00:13:16.915
refine the scenario, and export the investigation.

00:13:17.042 --> 00:13:22.155
The engineering keeps source identity, generated claims, automatic screens, and independent validation distinct.

00:13:22.281 --> 00:13:23.840
This concludes the recorded walkthrough.

00:13:23.967 --> 00:13:29.965
The application, presentation, and evaluation materials are ready for a live discussion of the tradeoffs and next validation steps.
